Mobs do not just show up. You assemble them. That is the joke and the progression.

The book splits into chapters. Mechanical Genesis is Create basics. Organic Synthesis is pulp to biomass. Artificial Life is fermented mass and eggs. Ecology Engine is the first spawn egg and the farm. The Deep is Deeper Darker. The True End is dust, frames, eyes. Later chapters hang off those.

A typical line: mix organic mass, bottle it, run a sequenced assembly, get an egg, decide if you even want that mob in your world. Sixty-plus spawn egg recipes exist for a reason. You pick the neighbors.

End portal frames are crafted. Eyes too. When the book says The True End follows The Deep, it means that. Do not dig for a stronghold.

If a mixing recipe fails, you are probably missing a KubeJS item the pack registers on purpose (wax, tentacle, brass dust). The quest text is usually sitting on that item. Read it before you rewrite the script.
